# Plain-text formulas (no LaTeX)

This repo is published with MkDocs Material. MathJax/KaTeX is not enabled. Do not use LaTeX (`\[ \]`, `\( \)`, `$$`, `\text{}`, `\frac{}`). It renders as raw markup.

In docs, README, comments, and user-facing text, use a fenced `text` block or a single-line expression with Unicode where helpful (`Δ`, subscripts as `_current`).

```text
# BAD — will not render
\[
\text{TTE} = \frac{\text{Capacity} - \text{Used}_{\text{current}}}{\left(\frac{\Delta \text{Used}}{\Delta t}\right)}
\]
If \(\Delta \text{Used} / \Delta t \le 0\), skip the alert.

# GOOD
TTE = (Capacity - Used_current) / (ΔUsed / Δt)
```

If the fill rate is zero or negative (usage is flat or shrinking), do not emit an exhaustion alert.

Match the worker chapter style: name the symbols in a following sentence rather than wrapping them in `\text{...}`.
